  "summary": "A metering (dosing) pump delivers a precise, adjustable volume per stroke. Here a motor turns a worm gear and eccentric that reciprocate a plunger; the plunger does not touch the chemical but pushes on hydraulic oil, which flexes a PTFE diaphragm evenly. As the diaphragm retracts, the suction ball valves open and the head fills; as it advances, they close and the discharge balls lift. Output is set by stroke length (knob) and stroke rate, typically with repeatability of the order of ±1 % — used for chemical injection, water treatment and process dosing where leakage of hazardous chemicals must be avoided.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive displacement – reciprocating",
    "configuration": "Hydraulically actuated diaphragm metering pump (API 675 type), simplex"
  },
